Patch 1 has just install-mail make INBOX, Next, Later, and Archive, as
well as sent. I could not reproduce the core dump with isync 1.5.1
here. If you still have the core, or remember which folders were
there when it crashed, I can look further.

I found a related failure instead. By default mbsync keeps its sync
state in ~/.local/state/isync, apart from the folders. When the mail
root is removed or made again, that state no longer matches, and
every sync fails with "Unable to recover from UIDVALIDITY change".
lab-claude had such state from an earlier sync. Patch 2 keeps
lab-claude's state in each folder. I left beastie's config alone,
since your sync there runs both ways and already has state. Moving
that state would make mbsync copy every message to the other side.

